    {
      "id": "bb071fef-2e67-4ccb-b451-2bf373f090fb",
      "name": "Setup and delivery notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        5060,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 1000,
        "content": "# Track competitor Google ads in Google Sheets with Apify\n\n## Who is this for?\n\nMarketing analysts who want a repeatable, bounded log of a competitor's Google ads without maintaining scraper infrastructure.\n\n## What it does\n\nThe workflow reads saved keys, launches one Apify Actor, waits for completion, checks HEALTH/TARGETS and upserts records into Google Sheets. An empty scope starts a baseline. Later unseen IDs are logged; first-seen time does not prove publication time. Older rows are retained.\n\n## Setup\n\nCreate a private Ads tab using the supplied CSV headers. Import the inactive workflow. In Configuration, set your spreadsheet ID and Actor input. Connect Header Auth on five Apify HTTP nodes and Google Sheets OAuth2 on both Sheets nodes. Run manually twice, inspect reports and check stable keys before activating the daily 09:00 UTC schedule. Keep Start Actor's Execute Once enabled and run sequentially.\n\n## Requirements and customization\n\nUse your own Apify account/token and Google spreadsheet edit access. Defaults: one domain, US, 20 ads, details off, Actor tracking off and a $0.10 Actor charge cap. Hosting and other service costs are separate. Change the domain/region for your use case; each filter scope establishes its own baseline.\n\nTested on self-hosted n8n 2.26.4. Other environments need validation. This is not a complete competitor inventory and sends no notifications.\n\n[Setup guide and headers](https://github.com/Datasmith-lab/datasmithlab-google-ads-n8n#setup)\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4dfffd99-1a6d-4563-9fdc-14fe55fa03ab",
      "name": "Daily 09 UTC",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 9 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "9b6b07ee-8de1-42e9-a99e-8b7d68b6817c",
      "name": "1 \u00b7 Open Actor & prepare Ads tab",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -600,
        -500
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 500,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## 1. Prepare your accounts\n[Open Google Ads Transparency Scraper on Apify](https://apify.com/datasmithlab/google-ads-transparency-scraper)\nCheck Actor access and pricing.\nCreate a private Sheet with a tab named **Ads**.\nPaste ads-sheet-headers.csv into row 1.\nKeep this imported workflow inactive."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "14807c88-2ed5-4d2c-9df4-08f52922ff89",
      "name": "2 \u00b7 Configure your snapshot",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -50,
        -500
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 500,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## 2. Open Configuration (Edit Fields)\nReplace **REPLACE_WITH_SPREADSHEET_ID** in the spreadsheetId field with the text between /d/ and /edit in your Sheet URL.\nSet one lowercase domain and region.\nStart with maxItems=20, maxAdsPerTarget=20.\nKeep onlyNewAds=false: Sheets stores observed IDs.\nDefault Actor charge cap: $0.10; check current prices."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a7a0646d-c699-406a-b2c2-de8213dc60d9",
